#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Buchhwin Control Center — the settings GUI.

The point of this application: change how the desktop looks and behaves without
opening a text editor. Keys, borders, gaps, blur, theme, wallpaper, input,
idle timings and autostart.

How it talks to Hyprland
------------------------
It reads and writes ~/.config/hypr/settings.lua — plain data — and then reloads
the compositor. It never parses hand-written Lua, and it never edits
hyprland.lua, binds.lua or rules.lua.

`hyprctl keyword` is not an option: with a Lua config provider it does not work
(hyprctl(1) says so outright). So "apply" means write the file and
`hyprctl reload`. That is slightly slower than a keyword call and has the large
advantage of surviving the next reload, which a keyword call does not.
"""

